  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37143888",
      "title": "Which Problem Do Keys Solve?",
      "lectureOrder": 150,
      "videoOrder": 138,
      "sourceHash": "1df27d0688a6930d949048e633279fbca9308c4d3cc6ebcfca725f17a1c71def",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 5.64,
          "en": "Now to understand what the idea behind keys is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.64,
          "end": 9.09,
          "en": "and when we need keys, let's come back to this concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.09,
          "end": 11.37,
          "en": "of widget and element trees,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.37,
          "end": 13.86,
          "en": "because you learned that every widget gets its element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 16.23,
          "en": "That's what we covered in the last lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.23,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "Now what happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 21.09,
          "en": "to those elements if two widgets change their place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.09,
          "end": 23.34,
          "en": "as we're doing it in this Todo app?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.34,
          "end": 24.84,
          "en": "There when we reorder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.84,
          "end": 27.87,
          "en": "our widgets, these widgets change their place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.87,
          "end": 30.33,
          "en": "They're not staying in the same position.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.33,
          "end": 31.38,
          "en": "So what happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.38,
          "end": 35.22,
          "en": "to those elements if those widgets change their place?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.22,
          "end": 39.63,
          "en": "Well, the element skeleton actually stays the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.63,
          "end": 41.79,
          "en": "We keep the same element structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.79,
          "end": 46.38,
          "en": "and indeed Flutter does not create new elements here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.38,
          "end": 48.99,
          "en": "Instead, it only updates which element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.99,
          "end": 51.27,
          "en": "refers to which widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.27,
          "end": 54.72,
          "en": "And Flutter does this for performance reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.72,
          "end": 58.8,
          "en": "It simply sees that even though something changed related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.8,
          "end": 62.58,
          "en": "to the widgets, it's still the same amount of widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.58,
          "end": 65.1,
          "en": "and the same type of widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 68.97,
          "en": "Because here in this list, when we reorder our Todo's,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.97,
          "end": 72.39,
          "en": "we might be changing the order of some TodoItems,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.39,
          "end": 75.78,
          "en": "but we still have the same amount of TodoItems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.78,
          "end": 79.71000000000001,
          "en": "and we also still have the same kind of widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.71000000000001,
          "end": 83.78999999999999,
          "en": "We have three TodoItems, even though their text might",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.78999999999999,
          "end": 85.68,
          "en": "have changed position.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.68,
          "end": 88.62,
          "en": "But for that reason, to optimize performance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.62,
          "end": 92.88,
          "en": "Flutter does indeed not throw away those existing TodoItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.88,
          "end": 96.69,
          "en": "elements and recreate them, but instead it reuses them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.69,
          "end": 101.69,
          "en": "But it keeps track of which element refers to which widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.97,
          "end": 104.78999999999999,
          "en": "To make sure that in the end, the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.78999999999999,
          "end": 106.86,
          "en": "that might be displayed inside of a widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.86,
          "end": 108.06,
          "en": "So the icon widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.06,
          "end": 110.25,
          "en": "and the text widget that is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.25,
          "end": 113.16,
          "en": "for outputting the TodoItem specific data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.16,
          "end": 116.22,
          "en": "that those things can be updated on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.22,
          "end": 118.53,
          "en": "To make sure that this is possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.53,
          "end": 121.59,
          "en": "Flutter connects every element to a widget and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.59,
          "end": 123.78,
          "en": "therefore here it reuses the elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 126.6,
          "en": "but updates the references",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.6,
          "end": 130.56,
          "en": "so that therefore the nested elements that were created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.56,
          "end": 132.09,
          "en": "for these TodoItems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.09,
          "end": 134.79,
          "en": "So in this case here, the element for the icon widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.79,
          "end": 136.98,
          "en": "the element for the SizedBox widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.98,
          "end": 140.22,
          "en": "and the element for the text widget can be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.22,
          "end": 143.79,
          "en": "to reflect the correct TodoItem data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.79,
          "end": 146.1,
          "en": "That is in the end what happens in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.1,
          "end": 149.4,
          "en": "where some Todo's might be shuffled around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.4,
          "end": 152.34,
          "en": "Now, why is this important to understand?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.34,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "Because here it explains what happens behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.49,
          "end": 158.85,
          "en": "And as you can see here, the app works absolutely correctly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.85,
          "end": 161.97,
          "en": "and displays the intended result despite Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.97,
          "end": 163.56,
          "en": "reusing those elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.56,
          "end": 165.12,
          "en": "So we have the best of both worlds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.12,
          "end": 168.633,
          "en": "We have good performance and display the intended result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.8,
          "end": 174.21,
          "en": "but things start to break at least without keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.21,
          "end": 177.69299999999998,
          "en": "if we make one important change inside of key start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.62,
          "end": 180.54,
          "en": "If we replace TodoItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.54,
          "end": 182.88,
          "en": "which is coming from the TodoItem Dart file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.88,
          "end": 186.3,
          "en": "with the CheckableTodoItem widget here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.3,
          "end": 188.02,
          "en": "by using CheckableTodoItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.63,
          "end": 194.16,
          "en": "and updating the imports to import CheckableTodoItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 195.753,
          "en": "and get rid of this import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.68,
          "end": 197.89,
          "en": "If we do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.32,
          "end": 201.45,
          "en": "and we restart the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.45,
          "end": 205.5,
          "en": "we see that we now can mark these Todo's as completed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.5,
          "end": 207,
          "en": "But what you will notice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207,
          "end": 209.16,
          "en": "is that if I only check the first one here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.16,
          "end": 213.54,
          "en": "and I then change the order, that looks broken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.54,
          "end": 215.79,
          "en": "The first Todo is still checked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.79,
          "end": 219.54,
          "en": "But of course this technically is now a different Todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 219.54,
          "end": 221.85,
          "en": "So now here we have a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.85,
          "end": 225.18,
          "en": "because even though Flutter does indeed manage element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 225.18,
          "end": 228.21,
          "en": "references, so references to widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.21,
          "end": 231.12,
          "en": "and even though it updates those references,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 231.12,
          "end": 234,
          "en": "state is managed in a different way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234,
          "end": 236.19,
          "en": "And here we are dealing with state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 236.19,
          "end": 238.47,
          "en": "because in the CheckableToDo widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.47,
          "end": 240.69,
          "en": "we indeed have a StatefulWidget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 240.69,
          "end": 244.293,
          "en": "And there we are managing this Checked State in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 245.28,
          "end": 247.95,
          "en": "And we're getting this broken result here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 247.95,
          "end": 250.62,
          "en": "because these state objects that belong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 250.62,
          "end": 254.52,
          "en": "to widgets are managed as independent objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 254.52,
          "end": 258.18,
          "en": "that are connected to the elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 258.18,
          "end": 259.98,
          "en": "And this actually makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 259.98,
          "end": 263.7,
          "en": "because we also do have separate state classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 263.7,
          "end": 267.27,
          "en": "So indeed we also get separate objects in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 267.27,
          "end": 269.34,
          "en": "And before in the course I mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 269.34,
          "end": 272.37,
          "en": "that those state objects would be connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 272.37,
          "end": 274.26,
          "en": "to the widget objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 274.26,
          "end": 277.77,
          "en": "Well, technically that's not entirely correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 277.77,
          "end": 280.65,
          "en": "Instead, those state objects are connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 280.65,
          "end": 284.073,
          "en": "to the element objects that are connected to the widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 285.06,
          "end": 288.12,
          "en": "Now, if widgets change their place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 288.12,
          "end": 291,
          "en": "as mentioned, Flutter reuses elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 291,
          "end": 295.65,
          "en": "and just updates the references, the pointers to widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 295.65,
          "end": 298.86,
          "en": "but the state objects don't move around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 298.86,
          "end": 302.46,
          "en": "So here you can see that when TodoItem A and B",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 302.46,
          "end": 303.87,
          "en": "change the place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 303.87,
          "end": 307.41,
          "en": "the state's A and B stay in their places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 307.41,
          "end": 310.38,
          "en": "And that now suddenly connects the TodoItem B",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 310.38,
          "end": 312,
          "en": "with the State A here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 312,
          "end": 315.39,
          "en": "because the state don't move together with the widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 315.39,
          "end": 317.67,
          "en": "Instead, they are connected to the elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 317.67,
          "end": 321.99,
          "en": "which also didn't move around, but which instead were reused",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 321.99,
          "end": 323.13,
          "en": "and stayed in place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 323.13,
          "end": 326.19,
          "en": "and just got their widget references updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 326.19,
          "end": 328.05,
          "en": "And that's of course a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 328.05,
          "end": 331.533,
          "en": "But it is a problem that is solved with help of keys.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
